<head>
<no>1</no><heading id="sec.1-he"
guid="_20512af1-12f6-4a9a-b23c-3ef263c6bede"><b>Name of
Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
refid="act-1998-100" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Commonwealth
Places (Mirror Taxes Administration) Act
1998</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dab7eeb7-4eb7-42f4-ae55-84ce0bbc924b"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading id="sec.2-he"
guid="_488a0146-aace-4a02-a7d8-1cc1987660f5"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e7950bd0-0928-43ec-a39a-f6d5e98c5ea7"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on a day or days to be
appointed by proclamation, except as provided by subsection
(2).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_32d25b46-3be4-470c-be87-56cfe7e4356c"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">When an arrangement has been made with the
Commonwealth under section 5, section 7 is deemed to have come into operation
on 6 October 1997.</txt></block></tier>

<note id="sec.2-note" guid="_024a0b42-245e-49fa-ac6b-d7306f44fde1"
type="legtext"><heading id="sec.2-note-he"
guid="_9224087c-8e42-4e6d-9e55-e7510e1c6eff"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">The operation of this Act and the Commonwealth
Act will depend on the making of an arrangement under section 5 of this Act
and section 9 of the Commonwealth Act. As soon as the arrangement is made, the
State taxing laws are taken to have always applied in relation to Commonwealth
places in the State, but not so as to impose any liability for tax for things
that happened before 6 October 1997.</txt></block></note>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fd22c439-7218-40da-adba-2384ec9773c1"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading id="sec.3-he"
guid="_a99f84a7-04cf-40d3-8602-465611eec542"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_49ba68fa-e6b0-457b-9f10-e73419703cdc"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.appliedlaw"
guid="_74ffafd2-f224-4318-9440-64111ab55f44" type="definition"><b><i>applied
law</i></b></defterm> means the provisions of a State taxing law that apply in
relation to a Commonwealth place in accordance with the Commonwealth
Act.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.CommonwealthAct"
guid="_071bf991-47e9-413e-878e-f11a18c2445b"
type="definition"><b><i>Commonwealth Act</i></b></defterm> means the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Commonwealth
Places (Mirror Taxes) Act 1998</i></name></legref> of the
Commonwealth.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.Commonwealthplace"
guid="_dfd77a75-ba7f-4308-b871-6a9e2e74df10"
type="definition"><b><i>Commonwealth place</i></b></defterm> means a place in
the State (not being the seat of Government) acquired by the Commonwealth for
public purposes.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.CommonwealthConstitution"
guid="_36a2077c-39fa-4bfc-b6d0-d42c55b7b723"
type="definition"><b><i>Commonwealth Constitution</i></b></defterm> means the
<legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="no">Constitution of the Commonwealth</name></legref>.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.correspondingappliedlaw"
guid="_6569e1bd-2af9-46a5-bada-c68cb0a45af3"
type="definition"><b><i>corresponding applied law</i></b></defterm>, in
relation to a State taxing law, means an applied law that corresponds to the
State taxing law.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm
id="sec.3-def.excludedbysection52ioftheCommonwealthConstitution"
guid="_1433041f-dfe5-40a2-80f3-539517f876c2" type="definition"><b><i>excluded
by section 52 (i) of the Commonwealth Constitution</i></b></defterm> means
inapplicable by reason only of the operation of section 52 of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Commonwealth
Constitution</name></legref> in relation to Commonwealth
places.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.inrelationto"
guid="_54801f2c-57ab-4cc6-b827-ec3bc2848433" type="definition"><b><i>in
relation to</i></b></defterm>, when used in relation to a Commonwealth place
or a place that was a Commonwealth place, means in, or in relation to, the
Commonwealth place or former Commonwealth place.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.modifications"
guid="_b122bc17-8beb-4263-bb02-53fa17021a63"
type="definition"><b><i>modifications</i></b></defterm> includes additions,
omissions and substitutions.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.proceedings"
guid="_dbf40d62-2dcc-4197-9cf4-df55547987ac"
type="definition"><b><i>proceedings</i></b></defterm> means any proceedings,
whether civil or criminal and whether original or appellate.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.Stateauthority"
guid="_596495aa-2c3d-4eaa-8575-f7e6ffcdfae0" type="definition"><b><i>State
authority</i></b></defterm> means any of the following:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a" guid="_ba701afa-d34a-4ccb-a21a-739397f56b42"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Governor, a Minister or a member of the
Executive Council of the State,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b" guid="_3e700a22-323b-403d-8a74-1233614b5fa0"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a court of the State,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.c" guid="_1770be20-38f2-4bb0-8fcc-70f9f516df72"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a person who holds office as a member of a court
of the State,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.d" guid="_e75d5f87-c1fa-4785-9553-190e9a3de8cf"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a body created by or under the law of the
State,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.e" guid="_416e741d-40b6-47a3-ac49-3b9fdd4ec69e"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an officer or employee of the State, or of a body
referred to in paragraph (d).</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.Statelaw"
guid="_2123ef18-3b85-4955-8153-a7ea9257e09e" type="definition"><b><i>State
law</i></b></defterm> means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a-oc.2"
guid="_cdfca4a7-5de9-4533-a3be-038dfccf0e9b" provision.type="other"
affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any law in force in the State, whether written or
unwritten, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b-oc.2"
guid="_d47bef31-a618-46b3-99ae-98ea6a944fbd" provision.type="other"
affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any instrument made or having effect under a law
referred to in paragraph (a),</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">but does not include a law of the Commonwealth, whether
written or unwritten, or an instrument made or having effect under such a
law.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.3-def.Statetaxinglaw"
guid="_eb1321bc-5d1e-4d2b-a453-596d9a199842" type="definition"><b><i>State
taxing law</i></b></defterm> means a State law that is a State taxing law
within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6f59c811-d725-4b00-9b40-db4a5b1ac607"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The note after section 2 does not form part of
this Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d8aaf397-204b-4cda-855c-77320795ad0f"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading id="sec.4-he"
guid="_9b134597-4f08-408e-9cc6-e31b3a59a5d7"><b>This Act binds the
Crown</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act binds the Crown in right of the State
and, in so far as the legislative power of the State permits, in all its other
capacities.</txt></block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_921b5409-1145-4dc2-b796-80c85c12f076"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading id="pt.2-he"
guid="_b5c4eb2a-1bf6-48af-bbb4-6ccaa57d6294"><b>Administration and operation
of State taxing laws as applied laws in relation to Commonwealth
places</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_25a516b8-e4a3-4a74-8cb2-25ed6d59cc54"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading id="sec.5-he"
guid="_21f8a733-d730-4645-a305-77edc3ff4c5c"><b>Arrangements with
Commonwealth</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_89e55b19-43bd-4c30-a105-fd7dda5e8b76"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make an arrangement with the
Governor-General of the Commonwealth in relation to the exercise or
performance of a power, duty or function (not being a power, duty or function
involving the exercise of judicial power) by a State authority under an
applied law.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8cf1f18b-890e-4a0c-9ef8-071ea8ae49aa"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may arrange with the
Governor-General for the variation or revocation of an arrangement made under
this section.</txt></block></tier>

<note id="sec.5-note" guid="_96dd1fb4-9d04-4706-858d-faebb5479122"
type="editorial"><heading id="sec.5-note-he"
guid="_8ef68931-4cad-4c8f-9577-119501bf9d39"><b>Editorial
note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">For an arrangement under this section see
Commonwealth Gazette No GN 7 of 20.2.2002, p 590</txt></block></note>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_48fe7fbf-05ec-4713-bdba-cab3c33661f5"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading id="sec.6-he"
guid="_2fae9f76-1df1-40d9-98c3-abd4c81e0cfa"><b>Exercise of powers etc by
State authorities</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Despite any State law, a State authority has any
power, duty or function that the Commonwealth Act authorises or requires the
authority to exercise or perform.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2e99e046-9841-4300-8596-f069c3e3435f"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading id="sec.7-he"
guid="_30b857cd-7a84-4b4e-b52b-aa929b4f0a41"><b>Modified operation of State
taxing laws</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f9dc930b-02f0-4dad-a1e6-0ffa717974df"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If, in relation to a State taxing law, there is a
corresponding applied law, the State taxing law is to be read and construed
with any modifications that are necessary or convenient:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a" guid="_7daecc16-5227-492d-8805-1237ce7a3b8e"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">for the purpose of enabling the effective
operation of the State taxing law in conjunction with the corresponding
applied law, or</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b" guid="_5c9a8184-f550-4fc4-be57-be653e20d3e7"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">for the purpose of enabling the State taxing law
to operate so that a taxpayer has a combined liability under:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b-para2.i"
guid="_da2f1f7e-e14a-43a3-83fa-d1627ba27c16" provision.type="other"
affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the State taxing law, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b-para2.ii"
guid="_6f91d464-6752-41c9-87a8-d4011a5f1b40" provision.type="other"
affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the corresponding applied
law,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">that is as nearly as possible the same as the
taxpayer&#8217;s liability would be under the State taxing law alone if the
Commonwealth places in the State were not Commonwealth
places.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b6befcd0-6de4-4d52-9f27-512b75f84b36"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Regulations may prescribe particular
modifications that are to have effect under subsection
(1).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_eb858e3d-48ba-46d0-90f2-fd9c97726eea"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Modifications prescribed under subsection
(2):</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.a" guid="_4d4ea6ac-32c0-4922-8e91-2b27abc1345d"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">may be expressed to take effect from a day that
is earlier than the day on which the regulations are published in the Gazette
(but not earlier than 6 October 1997), and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.b" guid="_cd20d90f-2a01-4dd3-ab10-468790b437aa"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">may deal with the circumstances in which the
modifications apply, and with matters of a transitional or savings
nature.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1b07c1a9-d7a8-4886-9061-a80c8af72a1a"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading id="pt.3-he"
guid="_2b710777-c5a5-46f4-b457-79f5e60e5910"><b>Proceedings</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1d966465-6e94-4073-88d0-4ea1af9fabbe"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading id="sec.8-he"
guid="_189a8cd1-5e0f-4154-ae87-46ca77530018"><b>Continuation of proceedings if
place found not to be a Commonwealth place</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.8-para1.a" guid="_0485d781-379f-4b38-b004-fb6861a79ee9"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">proceedings have been commenced in a court under
a law as an applied law, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.8-para1.b" guid="_53606479-17b5-48d0-af00-70a157b26089"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the court is satisfied that the State taxing law
that corresponds to that law is not excluded by section 52 (i) of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Commonwealth
Constitution</name></legref>,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">then the proceedings must be continued as though they
had been commenced under the State taxing law.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2869910d-2bf6-4579-8403-ec6e4884d9d2"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading id="sec.9-he"
guid="_f9f380cf-1fce-4578-b459-e694a90ea154"><b>Objection not allowable on
ground of duplicate proceedings</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In any proceedings under a State taxing law, an
objection must not be allowed merely on the ground that proceedings have been
commenced, or are pending, under a corresponding applied
law.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a515ec6f-dd28-4c40-881b-6188797cede5"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading id="sec.10-he"
guid="_e751f35f-a1dd-4001-9e7e-1c6801fda5c4"><b>Proceedings on certain
appeals</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9df9d414-e916-48cf-9d6b-b7b81a65837b"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section applies to an appeal from a
judgment, decree, order or sentence of a court in proceedings under a law as
an applied law.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2643a2eb-9939-4e41-b851-7e959ca6fa7b"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If the court is satisfied that the State taxing
law that corresponds to that law is not excluded by section 52 (i) of the
<legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="no">Commonwealth Constitution</name></legref>, then the court must
deal with the appeal as though:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_a5a84484-d49a-4abb-9962-20957ffa3533"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the proceedings in relation to which the appeal
was brought had been brought under the State taxing law,
and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_e683c4c6-d3e7-4c25-87ec-e7cf118a33d4"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the judgment, decree, order or sentence had been
given or made in proceedings brought under the State taxing
law.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_476a94a4-91b0-4f06-88e5-9a965c72268b"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading id="sec.11-he"
guid="_baffffb9-673e-43f2-b985-28cfa59f50b5"><b>Certificates about ownership
of land</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_47b608fc-412f-44ad-bb4d-b859f4fdfa82"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In proceedings under a State taxing law (or
purporting to be under a State taxing law) in which any question arises as to
whether a place is a Commonwealth place, a certificate in writing given by an
authorised person about any of the following matters relating to land is
evidence of the matters stated in the certificate:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.11-ssec.1-para1.a" guid="_12ef6bd8-c11f-4d76-bc0b-cd67080e736f"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the ownership of the land, or of an estate or
interest in the land, on a date or during a period specified in the
certificate,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.11-ssec.1-para1.b" guid="_c8927212-8f79-484b-8541-62731f2f4325"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the existence and ownership of a right in respect
of the land, on a date or during a period specified in the
certificate.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c15e18b2-ae59-407b-b970-1a60ba2ee61e"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A document that purports to be a certificate
referred to in subsection (1) is to be regarded as being such a certificate,
and to have been duly given, unless the contrary is
proved.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_231e3043-d46b-4cc1-9457-ce192f5387f9"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="sec.11-def.authorisedperson"
guid="_256ee15c-a150-4bed-96d8-1499bc51cd92"
type="definition"><b><i>authorised person</i></b></defterm> has the same
meaning as it has in section 16 of the Commonwealth
Act.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_74ed7ef5-bb4d-42c3-9560-f808e097d250"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 4</b></no><heading id="pt.4-he"
guid="_4a7f83ad-94ab-4c72-9fe4-65d58b5195f1"><b>Validation and
saving</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.12">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2291a3dd-727c-4629-b2ea-7b605cd576bc"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>12</no><heading id="sec.12-he"
guid="_f826c1f9-e106-42f6-a058-7afc11bdba69"><b>Validation of things
purportedly done under an applied law</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.12-para1.a" guid="_1a541e1e-0eab-4196-9447-a78deda34321"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">something purports to have been done under a law
as an applied law, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.12-para1.b" guid="_6978b8b9-45e2-4db3-be45-a7bc18ba5614"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the State taxing law that corresponds to that law
is not excluded by section 52 (i) of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Commonwealth
Constitution</name></legref>,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">then that thing is to be regarded as having been done
under the State taxing law.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.13">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_064130b4-13e2-494b-abeb-6a9dc6cecc06"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>13</no><heading id="sec.13-he"
guid="_ed85ed4b-e1b5-4fb0-8466-0c01ac800d30"><b>Provisions as to operation of
applied law and State taxing law if a place ceases to be a Commonwealth
place</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d7f7e416-9329-4e09-bebd-eb1eb5ac8693"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section applies if an applied law ceases, or
ceased, to have effect in relation to a place at a particular time because the
place ceases, or ceased, to be a Commonwealth place at that
time.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e50ffa95-d70d-4656-823b-ccfb50af4613"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The State taxing law to which the applied law
corresponded immediately before that time:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.13-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_a28b2385-1231-471b-a807-24deb512ba34"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">applies, or is to be regarded as having applied,
in relation to that place from that time, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.13-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_83c01ce7-e6ea-4b28-8ad0-7e51c4833533"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">is to be read and construed as though it provided
expressly that it was intended to apply in relation to that place from that
time.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0458fbea-1983-4347-bb1e-054b571c1754"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following things are not affected:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.13-ssec.3-para1.a" guid="_037fe2da-5baf-4f68-99d3-521684fdab12"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any right, privilege, obligation or liability
acquired, accrued or incurred under the applied law,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.13-ssec.3-para1.b" guid="_891d5de8-8608-4986-b0a6-ccf683ce86f5"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in
respect of an offence against the applied law,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.13-ssec.3-para1.c" guid="_4866f885-4fd3-4712-8c54-779dcc8fc7c1"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in
respect of any right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or
punishment referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bcde6a2b-9a15-461a-8a34-8723f088b775"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any penalty, forfeiture or punishment referred to
in subsection (3) (b) may be imposed as if the applied law had not ceased to
have effect.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.5"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_87a9db52-f9a9-47eb-902a-47a411e45088"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An investigation, legal proceeding or remedy
referred to in subsection (3) (c) may be instituted, continued or enforced as
if the applied law had not ceased to have effect.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.14">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ccd28a57-78bf-4dfc-bc35-f0ab830efc2b"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>14</no><heading id="sec.14-he"
guid="_946f9a04-f873-4f1d-8796-817581897ee2"><b>Provisions as to operation of
State taxing law if a place becomes a Commonwealth place</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7060b057-0791-4f42-ab19-2862868b1322"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section applies if a State taxing law
ceases, or ceased, to have effect in relation to a place at a particular time
because the place becomes, or became, a Commonwealth place at that
time.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d4df12d5-4f7d-44af-ad1e-ac39daf6a180"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following things are not affected:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.14-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_c97abc36-a125-48b6-af06-0b17015f11e6"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the previous operation of the State taxing law
before that time,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.14-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_bf1040ef-5507-47e6-b8d9-03e7389073e8"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any right, privilege, obligation or liability
acquired, accrued or incurred under the State taxing law,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.14-ssec.2-para1.c" guid="_938e0e93-6056-40e1-b440-47c8c2b504b6"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in
respect of an offence against the State taxing law,</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.14-ssec.2-para1.d" guid="_bc110d17-699d-412f-ac01-5e8cef8ad63e"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in
respect of any right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or
punishment referred to in paragraph (b) or (c).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5e5021a8-f237-430b-b30f-f5ac9aaa6bfa"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any penalty, forfeiture or punishment referred to
in subsection (2) (c) may be imposed as if the State taxing law had not ceased
to have effect.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_65e5d277-9501-4e82-bda5-0922845a33fa"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An investigation, legal proceeding or remedy
referred to in subsection (2) (d) may be instituted, continued or enforced as
if the State taxing law had not ceased to have effect.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.5"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cbf8d177-4b97-43f6-b253-8cacf4bff661"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 5</b></no><heading id="pt.5-he"
guid="_324c78f2-44a9-48b9-9b59-5be8e2db5601"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.15">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9cdc2cd9-cf78-481b-85b8-c0ca5113fd5c"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>15</no><heading id="sec.15-he"
guid="_0f2470f5-ac6e-44b6-8e29-a46fc400538f"><b>Instruments referring to
applied law</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.15-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3480d300-40d8-4f7a-9fdd-ae3bd96e2ea1"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section applies to an instrument or other
writing that relates to an act, matter or thing that has a connection with a
Commonwealth place.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.15-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_41ce9e35-e5e0-4246-86ca-31e7333aa7ec"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In so far as:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.15-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_936ea7d8-3336-42b3-9e2b-b9d9ac62d8db"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the instrument or writing contains a reference to
a law as an applied law, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.15-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_d226a8dc-6223-43e4-98e4-39d07acff3ad"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the State taxing law that corresponds to that law
is not excluded by section 52 (i) of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Commonwealth
Constitution</name></legref>,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">the reference has effect as if it were a reference to
the State taxing law.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.16">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.16"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c3db7cf0-d8e2-40ac-9b70-1c8dcf056a7c"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>16</no><heading id="sec.16-he"
guid="_3695d362-33fc-4379-923a-99db5eb89e4d"><b>Appropriation</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any liability of the State:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.16-para1.a" guid="_8e6d00f5-a8d8-4a26-a613-95b14b33b327"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to pay money to the Commonwealth to enable it to
comply with section 23 (1) of the Commonwealth Act, or</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.16-para1.b" guid="_8249b707-d1c8-4506-ab88-ace1ad031849"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">under an arrangement with the Commonwealth under
section 5,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">is to be met out of the Consolidated Fund which is
appropriated to the necessary extent.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.17">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.17"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4e5ca90a-3c70-4094-a9b9-472db04c973e"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>17</no><heading id="sec.17-he"
guid="_058945c8-161f-4b1b-a493-be6a1d5e99ec"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations prescribing all
matters that are necessary or convenient to be prescribed to give effect to
the purposes of this Act.</txt></block></level>
</level>
